    Key intermediates: mol_011, mol_013, mol_017, mol_023

  P2: Early nitrile-stage guanidination with hydantoin-mediated hydrolysis
    Description: Shares early guanidination with P1 but captures the final aminonitrile as a hydantoin before hydrolysis. The additional hydantoin branch is speculative and requires warmer hydrolysis with uncertain product survival.
    Reactions: rxn_001 -> rxn_002 -> rxn_003 -> rxn_005 -> rxn_006 -> rxn_010 -> rxn_012 -> rxn_014 -> rxn_017 -> rxn_018 -> rxn_020 -> rxn_021
    Key intermediates: mol_011, mol_013, mol_023, mol_025

  P3: Three-carbon aminoaldehyde guanidination with direct hydrolysis
    Description: Reduces the initial amino nitrile before guanidination. Cyanamide then traps the aminoaldehyde as the cyclic guanidino hemiaminal. Competition between productive guanidination and aminoaldehyde degradation is unresolved.
