    Description: Combines speculative guanidination of 3-aminopropanal with final hydantoin capture. It differs from P3 by a genuine carbamylation and ring-hydrolysis sequence, not by different bookkeeping for the same reaction.
    Reactions: rxn_001 -> rxn_002 -> rxn_004 -> rxn_007 -> rxn_006 -> rxn_010 -> rxn_012 -> rxn_014 -> rxn_017 -> rxn_018 -> rxn_020 -> rxn_021
    Key intermediates: mol_012, mol_013, mol_023, mol_025

  P5: First-cyanohydrin guanidination with direct hydrolysis
    Description: Forms the first cyanohydrin before introducing guanidine. This avoids exposing guanidine to the first nitrile reduction while retaining a single primary amine for guanidination; stability and trapping selectivity remain speculative.
