    Description: Pyruvate is reductively aminated to alanine, which transfers nitrogen to 2-oxoglutarate in a proposed Fe(II)-assisted step. Pyruvate regeneration is stoichiometric, not proof of a sustained catalytic cycle. This differs from P7 in donor preparation.
