    Description: An aminoacetonitrile precursor is trapped through Bucherer-Bergs-type chemistry as hydantoin, then hydrolyzed through hydantoic acid to glycine. The exact low-temperature formation conditions and geochemical hydrolysis implementation are extrapolative, explicitly lower-confidence portions of this pathway.
