    Description: Fe(0)/hydroxylamine chemistry supplies glycine from glyoxylate. Glycine must leave the reducing iron-containing mixture before entering the Cu(II)-promoted serine-forming stage. Hydroxylamine availability and effective environmental separation are major assumptions.
